Paint and hit-test positioned z-index auto/0 boxes in tree order at their stacking
context's step-8 layer (Roves; Blitz #1493).

Base: crates.io blitz-dom 0.3.0-beta.4 (DioxusLabs/blitz
92b11f1bd8ab7975411328b0406a95a09445b4e7, packages/blitz-dom), after 0001-0003.
Applied in support/blitz-v8-probe/vendor/blitz-dom; see ROVES_PATCHES.md there.
Paired with patches/blitz-paint-0.3.0-beta.4/0001-cull-with-hoisted-content.patch.

Blitz painted a positioned z-index:auto box together with its whole subtree, so a
later positioned box nested in it (or in a static box) stayed below an earlier
`position: fixed; z-index: 0|auto` sibling hoisted to the root (CSS 2.1 Appendix E,
step 8 paints all of them in tree order). Positioned boxes are now lifted to the
enclosing stacking context's z-sorted list with z-index 0 and the list is sorted by
(z-index, tree order); paint (blitz-paint draw_children) and hit testing
(Node::hit_inner) already walk that list in matching opposite orders. Lifting stops at
boxes that clip (overflow, contain: paint, CSS clip, replaced/text inputs), at inline
roots, at sticky boxes and at relatively positioned flex/grid items.

